// StringLarge for the NeoDDS bounded-string LARGE-form interop probe (log-service Task 1 debt).
//
// NeoDDS's (:string N) member with N > 255 emits TI_STRING8_LARGE (0x71) + an LBound UInt32 in the
// TypeObject, versus TI_STRING8_SMALL (0x70) + an SBound octet for N <= 255. The SMALL form is on
// the externally-confirmed path (it carries the SBound field, value 0, for an unbounded string);
// the LARGE form has NEVER been exercised by a live peer. LogEvent bounds `message` at 1024, so it
// takes the LARGE path — this probe confirms the LARGE TypeObject framing interoperates before
// Phase B ships LogEvent.
//
// A real IDL string<1024> -> TI_STRING8_LARGE on this side, matching NeoDDS's (:string 1024). Same
// topic name "StringLarge", same registered type name "StringLarge", @key long id, so the bounded
// LARGE string is the only intended difference.

@final
struct StringLarge {
    @key long id;
    string<1024> text;
};
